<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Capabilities FinatriX asks Apple for. One entry here without the matching
  capability on the App ID in the Developer portal is a code-signing failure, so
  docs/IOS.md lists them side by side.

  `applinks:` is Universal Links — a finatrix.co link to one of the product's own
  screens (an email confirmation, a password reset, a shared guide) opens in the
  app instead of Safari. BOTH hosts are listed because iOS verifies each one
  separately against its own /.well-known/apple-app-site-association and does not
  follow redirects; www would silently fail to verify if it were left out. The
  Android twin of this is the autoVerify intent filter in AndroidManifest.xml.

  `webcredentials:` lets iOS offer the finatrix.co password already saved in the
  user's keychain when they sign in inside the app — less typing, and one less
  reason to pick a password weak enough to remember.

  `com.apple.developer.applesignin` is here although the app's own code never
  calls AuthenticationServices: Sign in with Apple runs through Supabase's OAuth
  flow in an SFSafariViewController, the same return leg Google uses. That flow
  is keyed on a Services ID (co.finatrix.signin), and Apple only lets a Services
  ID sign in on behalf of a PRIMARY App ID that has the Sign in with Apple
  capability. Automatic signing enables on the App ID what this file declares,
  so the requirement is recorded in the repository, where review sees it,
  instead of as a portal toggle nothing here mentions — losing it would break
  Apple sign-in for everyone with nothing in the app to show why. It also
  leaves the native sheet (docs/IOS.md §4.3) one plugin away.

  NOT here, deliberately:
    aps-environment                  No push notifications.
    com.apple.developer.icloud-*     No iCloud. Sync is Supabase's, so it works
                                     on Android and the web too.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:finatrix.co</string>
		<string>applinks:www.finatrix.co</string>
		<string>webcredentials:finatrix.co</string>
		<string>webcredentials:www.finatrix.co</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
